    <section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00004">
        <title>Solving Quadratics with Radical Solutions</title>
        <para id="para-00039">When solving quadratic equations, it is important to remember that:</para>
        <list id="list-00001">
          <item>Any positive number has two square roots, one positive and one negative, because there are two numbers that can be squared to make that number. (For example, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> both equal 36, so 6 and -6 are both square roots of 36.)</item>
          <item>The square root symbol <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mspace width="0.278em"/><m:mspace width="0.278em"/></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> can be used to express the positive square root of a number. For example, the square root of 36 is 6, but it can also be written as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>36</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math> because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>36</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>36</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
          <item>To express the negative square root of a number, say 36, we can write -6 or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>36</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
          <item>When a number is not a perfect square (for example, 40), we can express its square roots by writing <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>40</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>40</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
        </list>
        <para id="para-00040">How could we write the solutions to an equation like <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>? This equation is saying, “something squared is 11.” To make the equation true, that something must be <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00041">We can write:</para>
        <para id="para-00042"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>      or      <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00043"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>      or      <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00044">A more compact way to write the two solutions to the equation is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>11</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Solving Quadratics with Radical Solutions</title>
          <exercise id="exer-00006">
            <problem id="prob-00007">
              <para id="para-00045">Solve <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>17</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
              <para id="para-00046">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00007">
              <para id="para-00047">Here is how to solve this quadratic equation:</para>
              <para id="para-00048"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Make sure the quadratic is isolated on one side. </para><para id="para-00054"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>17</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00049"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Take the square root of both sides.</para><para id="para-00055"> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>17</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00050"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Simplify. </para><para id="para-00056"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>17</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00051"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Solve the equation. For this problem, add 2 to each side. </para><para id="para-00057"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>±</m:mi><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>17</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00052"><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - Simplify. </para><para id="para-00058"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>17</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>17</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
